From 37117e3adabaed2b4fe1e3a8d6aca72684427c7f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 23:19:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HOMEMON: the web Home Monitor is live -- home.* tags from
 golden's runtime TfHome, and Abort Home runs golden sbAbortHomeClick

- JsonBridge/ChanHome.{h,cpp} (new, wb_serve): W906_StageHomeMonitor stages home.fShow / home.fAbort / home.step /
  home.resetOk / home.rows / home.log / home.log.count, only while some browser has the Home Monitor open or minimized
  (W906_PageStreamWanted("home"), RULINGS_20260930 #12) or the home sequence shows it (fHome->fShow).  home.rows = the
  Visible THomeClass rows in vector order (labName Caption / Left / Top, edPos Text, ShowLed's lamp from W906_HomeLedState);
  home.log = the newest ListBox1 lines (newest first, capped at 100).  JSON through webbridge::JsonWriter (escapes, UTF-8 repair).
- act.home.abort -> golden TfHome::sbAbortHomeClick (uhome.cpp:4980-4986: GaliMotorServoOff + fAbort + Close), on the tick
  thread, only while fHome->fShow; otherwise refused "not-open: ..." with nothing called.  Dispatched in the main drain (ahead
  of the act.* catch-all) and in the three blocking-dialog waits like motor.stop; allowed while closing (CmdAllowedWhileClosing),
  exempt from the operator token (WebBridgeServer) and the anti-double-click guard (WebCmdGuard, stop direction).
- TfHome carries Panel2 (golden uhome.dfm "Reset OK" panel): GATE(W906-HOME-C2-PANEL2) lifted in Show() (golden :4846) and
  ProcessMotorHome case 1100 (golden :3516); display only.  Line counts of uhome.cpp / fHome.h / fHome.cpp / wb_serve.cpp /
  MainClose.cpp unchanged (same-line edits).
- ctest HomeMonitor (54 checks: rows / log JSON, escaping, the stage gate, abort happy path / not-open refusal / second press);
  MainCloseStop and WebCmdGuard pin the two allow-lists; FShow_Audit baseline +1 for the one deliberate direct fShow read.
- The web half (page/HW.home.html, page/ht9045_home_c.js, background.html MODAL_POLICY.home modeless) is delivered
  separately (the web tree is its own repository).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
